---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Clean Slate"
  description="The Terms & Conditions governing use of the Clean Slate website and the booking of our junk removal, cleanout, and hauling services."
>

  <Header />

  <main>

    <section>
      <div class="container max-w-3xl">

        <h1 class="mt-12 mb-2">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
        <p class="mb-10 text-sm text-muted">Last Updated: August 31, 2026</p>

        <div class="legal-prose text-body">

          <p>
            Welcome to Clean Slate Professional Clean Up Services
            (&ldquo;Clean Slate,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or
            &ldquo;our&rdquo;). These Terms &amp; Conditions govern your use of
            our website and your purchase or booking of junk removal, cleanout,
            hauling, and related services.
          </p>

          <p>
            By using our website or booking our services, you agree to these
            Terms &amp; Conditions.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Services</h2>
          <p>
            Clean Slate provides junk removal, furniture removal, appliance
            removal, cleanouts, construction cleanup, small demolition, and
            related services within our service area.
          </p>
          <p>
            Services and availability are subject to crew availability, property
            conditions, access, applicable laws, and our ability to safely
            perform the requested work.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Online Pricing</h2>
          <p>
            Prices displayed through our online booking system are based on the
            information, item selections, quantities, photos, and other details
            provided by the customer.
          </p>
          <p>
            Online pricing is an estimate of the expected service based on the
            information submitted. Our crew may verify the scope of work before
            beginning service.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the actual items, quantities, access conditions, or other
            circumstances differ significantly from the information submitted,
            Clean Slate may adjust the price. We will communicate any price
            adjustment before proceeding with the additional work.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Customer Responsibilities</h2>
          <p>
            Customers are responsible for providing accurate information when
            requesting or booking services.
          </p>
          <p>
            Customers must disclose relevant information about the items being
            removed, property access, stairs, long carrying distances, special
            conditions, and any other circumstances that may affect the work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unless otherwise agreed, items should be accessible and ready for
            removal when our crew arrives.
          </p>

          <h2>4. Access and Additional Work</h2>
          <p>
            Additional charges may apply when a job requires unexpected
            disassembly, excessive carrying, difficult access, stairs, unusual
            labor, or other work or conditions not reasonably reflected in the
            original booking.
          </p>
          <p>
            Clean Slate will communicate applicable additional charges before
            proceeding whenever reasonably possible.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Prohibited Materials</h2>
          <p>
            Clean Slate does not accept hazardous, illegal, or otherwise
            prohibited materials.
          </p>
          <p>
            Examples may include explosives, certain chemicals or fuels,
            asbestos-containing materials, medical waste, radioactive materials,
            and other materials restricted by law, disposal facilities, or Clean
            Slate.
          </p>
          <p>
            Customers are responsible for accurately identifying materials
            presented for removal.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are unsure whether we accept a particular item, contact us
            before booking.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Scheduling and Arrival Windows</h2>
          <p>
            Online booking times represent an arrival window rather than a
            guaranteed exact arrival time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Clean Slate will make reasonable efforts to arrive within the
            selected window but may experience delays due to traffic, weather,
            prior jobs, equipment issues, or circumstances outside our control.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Cancellations and Rescheduling</h2>
          <p>
            Cancellations or rescheduling requests made at least 24 hours before
            the scheduled service may be made without a cancellation charge.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cancellations, rescheduling requests, or no-shows with less than 24
            hours&rsquo; notice may result in forfeiture of any required deposit.
          </p>
          <p>
            If our crew has already been dispatched or has arrived at the
            property, additional charges may apply.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Deposits and Payment</h2>
          <p>Certain services may require a deposit.</p>
          <p>
            If a deposit is required, Clean Slate may send a payment request
            through our payment provider or Jobber.
          </p>
          <p>
            The remaining balance is due according to the payment terms provided
            to the customer.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Property and Damage</h2>
          <p>
            Customers are responsible for identifying valuable, fragile, or items
            requiring special handling before work begins.
          </p>
          <p>
            Clean Slate will use reasonable care when performing services.
            Customers should remove or secure valuables and personal property
            that are not part of the removal service.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Weather and Unsafe Conditions</h2>
          <p>
            Clean Slate may postpone or reschedule services when weather, road
            conditions, property conditions, materials, or other circumstances
            create an unsafe working environment.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will make reasonable efforts to contact customers regarding
            necessary schedule changes.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Photos and Information Submitted</h2>
          <p>
            Customers may submit photographs, descriptions, and other information
            to help Clean Slate evaluate and price requested services.
          </p>
          <p>
            Customers represent that they have the right to provide any
            photographs or information they submit.
          </p>

          <h2>12. Website Use</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to use this website lawfully and not to interfere with its
            operation, attempt unauthorized access, submit false information, or
            use the website for fraudulent or abusive purposes.
          </p>
          <p>
            We may modify website content, services, pricing, availability, or
            functionality at any time.
          </p>

          <h2>13. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>
            Our website may use third-party services for scheduling, payments,
            analytics, communications, hosting, maps, or other functionality.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your use of those services may also be subject to the third
            party&rsquo;s terms and privacy policies.
          </p>

          <h2>14. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Clean Slate will
            not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or
            unforeseeable damages arising from use of our website or services.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing in these Terms limits liability that cannot legally be
            limited under applicable law.
          </p>

          <h2>15. Changes to These Terms</h2>
          <p>
            Clean Slate may update these Terms &amp; Conditions from time to
            time. Updated terms will be posted on this website with a revised
            &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; date.
          </p>

          <h2>16. Governing Law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms &amp; Conditions are governed by the laws of the State of
            Iowa, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.
          </p>

          <h2>17. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these Terms or our services may be directed to Clean
            Slate Professional Clean Up Services through the contact information
            provided on our website.
          </p>

          <p>
            By using our website or booking our services, you acknowledge that
            you have read and agree to these Terms &amp; Conditions.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <Footer />

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--heading);
  }

  .legal-prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
